      "subject": "feat(governance): the records Chief Agent activation rests on are tracked in git (MS-2026-0007)",
      "body": "runtime-data was entirely git-ignored, yet every certification the activation gate depends on is re-derived from records there, so they existed only on the owner's Mac. Tested in a fresh clone: certifications re-derive only with the governed records, the replay designation, the designated Day-0 replay and its historical correlation, and the acquired conversations Day-0 coverage is re-proved from (owner decision: commit them). Those 31 files are now tracked in place through .gitignore exceptions, with no Runtime code change and no second copy. Other replays, correlations, browser recovery and test data stay ignored. npm run build now fails if any governed record would be ignored by git, including a newly designated replay. A fresh clone built from git alone shows the same activation and certification states as this machine; runtime suites 1569/1569 leave tracked records unchanged.\n\nMission: MS-2026-0007\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AHtXdN7VRusNxTFHzk5uFe",
